cartridge "HAWKMEN OF DINDRIN/E. V. AGUILAR JR., COMPUTE!/1983"

' THE HAWKMEN OF DINDRIN
' The game by Esteban V. Aguilar Jr. from COMPUTE!, June 1983 (pages
' 86-100; the notes on the Atari and Commodore 64 versions by Charles
' Brannon), for the ColecoVision in Amy by Amy Bienvenu. Ported by Claude
' (an AI made by Anthropic) for Amy Studio, 2026.
'
' Sources: the VIC-20 version (Programs 1 and 2), transcribed in
' orig/hawkmen-vic.bas from the scans beside it, gives the rules and the
' screen; the Atari and 64 versions (orig/hawkmen-atari.bas,
' orig/hawkmen-64.bas) give the shapes where the VIC's are plain: the
' hawkman flapping his wings, the grinning floaters, the lizards' darting
' tongues (two views each, flipped every 8 frames as those versions' machine
' language flips their two character sets), the oval stones and the wavy
' ground (art.py says which is which).
'
' The game: you, the hawkman, fly across the sky of Dindrin under the
' clouds, a row lower at each line's end. Left backs up, up climbs and
' down dives (diagonally, forward); no stick flies on. The button
' sticks out your tongue (three cells ahead): a floater is worth 15 points
' and 20 energy, the skimmer 5 and 10. Snatch the stones at the bottom (100
' points, 100 energy) but not where a lizard waits (it eats you and half
' your energy). Touching anything else costs a life; energy drains every
' move and the tongue costs 3; when energy is low (under 100) the border
' disappears. Four lives. The game goes on until the lives or the energy
' run out; then 10,000 points or more is a win.
'
' Controls (either joystick): the stick as above (right is not read, as
' on the VIC: flying on is the default), the button the tongue; after a
' game the button plays again, the stick down goes back to the credits.
'
' The VIC-20's screen (22 columns, 23 rows) is kept cell for cell, at
' columns 5-26 and rows 1-23, with its colour memory: each VIC character
' in each colour is a tile (art.py), so the name table holds the screen and
' its colours and the game reads PEEKs back from it. Y, SK, F and the
' other positions are the VIC's screen offsets (from 7680), Q its moves
' (+-1, +23, -21). Labels such as l51 are the listing's line numbers.
'
' Fixes (clear bugs of the listing; the original behaviour is noted where
' the code changes):
' - Line 58 printed the energy at column 1 of its row, over the word
'   ENERGY: (and a shorter number left old digits behind): it is printed
'   after ENERGY: here, cleared behind, and not below 0.
' - Line 57's floor test (Y+Q>=8163) made the last stone (column 21)
'   deadly: the floor starts at 8164.
' - Line 606 (the skimmer runs into you) moved Y one cell on (Y=Y+1)
'   without its colour address, so the burst landed beside you in the
'   wrong colour and your picture stayed: here the burst is on you.
' - Line 605 erased the skimmer's tail three cells back even just after
'   its wrap, cutting holes in the row above (row 17, columns 19-21).
' - Line 500 (flying into a lizard from the end of row 20) put a stone and
'   a lizard into the ground row: only cells of the stones' row change.
' - Lines 611-626 updated the border only when a floater appeared (one
'   pass in ten): it follows the energy every pass.
' - The tongue went on into the next row from the end of a line: it stops
'   at the line's end.
' - After a game the VIC kept the last text colour (purple, or red after a
'   win), so the next game's words, clouds and skimmer changed colour:
'   every game is drawn as the first.
' - Running out of energy with the tongue (line 101 to 500) left the
'   hawkman's picture where he was (a "ghost" that could be flown into):
'   it is erased.
' - The fire button still held when the game ended played again at once
'   (line 1035): it must be let go first.
'
' Improvements (smoother, more colour):
' - The hawkman is a sprite gliding from cell to cell over the pass (the
'   VIC jumped a cell at a time); the game still moves him by cells.
' - The tongue is red (the VIC drew it in whatever colour that cell's
'   colour memory held, mostly the blue of the empty sky).
' - The Atari and 64 shapes and their two-view animation (above).
'
' Liberties taken:
' - Timing: a pass of the main loop is 7 frames, about the VIC's BASIC
'   speed; each tongue step a frame, the burst after a catch 4 frames, the
'   crash 4, the lizard's meal 44 (its two pictures in turn).
' - The skimmer's head, multicolour on the VIC (colour 8), is drawn black.
' - Words in the ColecoVision's font; the score stops at 65535.
' - The title (Program 1's screen) waits for the button (the VIC loaded
'   Part 2 from tape meanwhile); a credits page with an original tune,
'   "Wings over Dindrin".
'
' House rules kept: text in columns 2-29; the frame loop is protected from
' the NMI and every screen is drawn with the NMI off after a wait.

const TSp0 = 128
const TSp1 = 129
const TSp2 = 130
const TSp3 = 131
const TSp4 = 132
const TSp5 = 133
const TSp6 = 134
const TSp7 = 135
const TFl0 = 136
const TFl1 = 137
const TFl2 = 138
const TFl3 = 139
const TFl4 = 140
const TFl5 = 141
const TFl6 = 142
const TFl7 = 143
const TLz0 = 144
const TLz1 = 145
const TLz2 = 146
const TLz3 = 147
const TLz4 = 148
const TLz5 = 149
const TLz6 = 150
const TLz7 = 151
const THawk = 152
const TTg0 = 153
const TTg1 = 154
const TTg2 = 155
const TTg3 = 156
const TTg4 = 157
const TTg5 = 158
const TTg6 = 159
const TTg7 = 160
const TSt0 = 161
const TSt1 = 162
const TSt2 = 163
const TSt3 = 164
const TSt4 = 165
const TSt5 = 166
const TSt6 = 167
const TSt7 = 168
const TCl0 = 169
const TCl1 = 170
const TCl2 = 171
const TCl3 = 172
const TCl4 = 173
const TCl5 = 174
const TCl6 = 175
const TCl7 = 176
const TBu0 = 177
const TBu1 = 178
const TBu2 = 179
const TBu3 = 180
const TBu4 = 181
const TBu5 = 182
const TBu6 = 183
const TBu7 = 184
const THd0 = 185
const THd1 = 186
const THd2 = 187
const THd3 = 188
const THd4 = 189
const THd5 = 190
const THd6 = 191
const THd7 = 192
const TJaw = 193
const TGnd = 194
const TNeck = 195
const Tg0 = 196
const Tg1 = 197
const Tg2 = 198
const Tg3 = 199
const Tg4 = 200
const Tg5 = 201
const Tg6 = 202
const Tg7 = 203
const Tg8 = 204
const Tg9 = 205
const TgL = 206
const TgI = 207
const TgF = 208
const TgE = 209
const TgCol = 210
const TgS = 211
const TgC = 212
const TgO = 213
const TgR = 214
const TgN = 215
const TgG = 216
const TgY = 217
const TgMin = 218
const NTilesG = 728
const PSpY = 128
const PSpR = 129
const PSpB = 130
const PB0 = 150
const NTilesP = 600
const PAFirst = 131
const PACount = 19
const TgFirst = 196
const TgCount = 23
const SndThrum = 1
const SndDive = 2
const SndClimb = 3
const SndStone = 4
const SndTongue = 5
const SndGulp = 6
const SndCrash = 7
const SndTuneA = 8
const SndTuneB = 9

' --- the listing's variables ----------------------------------------------
' Y the hawkman (VIC offset), Q his move (16 bits: -1 is 65535), E the
' energy (16 bits, signed: 32768 and up below zero), SC the score, TN the
' lives, SK the skimmer's head, F the floater's place, J the stick
' (the VIC's PEEK(37151): 126 none, 122 up, 118 down, 110 left, 94 fire)
u16 Y = 133
u16 Q = 0
u16 E = 200
u16 SC = 0
u8 TN = 4
u16 SK = 400
u16 F = 0
u8 J = 126
u8 O = 0
u8 D = 0
u8 Z = 0
u8 W = 0
u8 X = 0
u8 Bt = 0
' Go5: 1 when a subroutine jumps to line 500 (the crash), Hit: 1 when the
' skimmer ran into the hawkman
u8 Go5 = 0
u8 Hit = 0
' cells: B the VIC offset, Ch Cl the VIC character and colour to put, Kd
' Kc those found (PEEK), Tp the tile, Tl its tile
u16 B = 0
u16 Bw = 0
u8 Ch = 0
u8 Cl = 0
u8 Kd = 0
u8 Kc = 0
u8 Tp = 0
u8 Tl = 0
' Tc the text colour (VIC), Bord the border (0 red, 1 yellow)
u8 Tc = 6
u8 Bord = 0
' the random numbers (RND): a 16-bit xorshift
u16 Rs = $3A57
u16 Rt = 0
u16 Rw = 0
u16 Rv = 0
u32 Uq = 0
u32 Uq2 = 0
' TI$: Fr frames, Ts seconds since the game began
u8 Fr = 0
u16 Ts = 0
' the animation: Anim 1 when the game's tiles are loaded, Af the frames,
' Av the view (0 or 1)
u8 Anim = 0
u8 Af = 0
u8 Av = 0
' the hawkman's sprite: Hon 1 shown, Hx Hy its place, Gx Gy its goal
u8 Hon = 0
u8 Hx = 0
u8 Hy = 0
u8 Gx = 0
u8 Gy = 0
' for the test bot: Ph 1 credits, 2 title, 3 playing, 4 the game's end;
' Stp the passes; Jr the stick read in the pass
u8 Ph = 0
u8 Stp = 0
u8 Jr = 126
u8 Rb = 0
u8 Rd = 0
u8 V = 0
u8 V2 = 0
u8 Jp = 0
u8 Jh = 0
u8 Rr = 0
u8 Tick = 0
u16 NumW = 0
u8 Neg = 0
u8 Nd = 0
u8 Dg[5]
u8 Nc = 0
u8 Nr = 0
u16 Hh = 0
u16 Mm = 0
u8 Tcf = 0
u8 Tcn = 0

  tile screen
  sprites 8x8
  set sound table HkSoundTable areas 4
  nmi off
  copy SpritePat count 16 to vram.spr_pat
  set sprite count 1
  hide sprite 0
  update sprites
  screen on

l0:
  CreditsPage
  TitlePage
l6:
  ' 6-9: TI$ from zero, CLR (Q = 0), the energy
  Ts = 0
  Fr = 0
  Q = 0
  E = 200
  ' 10: the screen
  SC = 0
  Y = 133
  SK = 400
  TN = 4
  Bord = 0
  Tc = 6
  GameScreen
  Ph = 3
l50:
  ' 50: the hawkman (black) at his start
  B = Y
  Ch = 0
  Cl = 0
  call asm HkPut
  HawkGoal
  Hx = Gx
  Hy = Gy
  Hon = 1
l51:
  ' 51: the stick, a move's energy, the world (600)
  inc Stp
  Pace(7)
  Jr = J
  E = E - 1
  Go5 = 0
  Hit = 0
  World
  if Go5 = 1 then goto l500
l52:
  if J = 94 then
    Tongue
    if Go5 = 1 then goto l500
  end if
  if J = 110 then Q = 65535
  if J = 126 then Q = 1
  if J = 118 then
    Q = 23
    play sound SndDive
  end if
  if J = 122 then
    Q = 65515
    play sound SndClimb
  end if
l57:
  ' 57: off the field (above row 5, or the floor: see the fixes)
  B = Y
  Ch = 32
  PutKeep
  Bw = Y + Q
  if Bw < 110 then goto l500
  if Bw >= 484 then goto l500
l58:
  ShowStat
  ELe0
  if V = 1 then goto l1000
l59:
  B = Y + Q
  call asm HkGet
  if Kd = 35 then goto l90
  if Kd <> 32 then goto l500
l75:
  Y = Y + Q
  B = Y
  Ch = 0
  Cl = 0
  call asm HkPut
  HawkGoal
  B = Y + 22
  call asm HkGet
  if Kd = 36 then goto l300
  goto l51

l90:
  ' 90-96: a stone: 100 points and 100 energy; the hawkman takes it and
  ' rises a row
  Y = Y + Q
  B = Y
  Ch = 0
  Cl = 0
  call asm HkPut
  HawkGoal
  AddSc(100)
  E = E + 100
  play sound SndStone
  Hold(4)
  B = Y
  Ch = 32
  PutKeep
  Y = Y - 22
  B = Y
  Ch = 0
  Cl = 0
  call asm HkPut
  HawkGoal
  goto l51

l300:
  ' 300-351: a lizard eats the hawkman (red), then leaves a stone; half
  ' the energy, a life
  HawkOff
  B = Y + 22
  Cl = 2
  PutCol
  B = Y + 22
  Ch = 41
  PutKeep
  B = Y
  Ch = 36
  Cl = 2
  call asm HkPut
  play sound SndThrum
  for Rr = 1 to 22
    B = Y
    Ch = 36
    PutKeep
    Hold(1)
    B = Y
    Ch = 37
    PutKeep
    Hold(1)
  next
  B = Y
  Ch = 32
  PutKeep
  B = Y + 22
  Ch = 35
  PutKeep
  ' 346: E=INT(E*.5)
  if E >= 32768 then
    E = E >> 1
    E = E | 32768
  else
    E = E >> 1
  end if
  dec TN
  if TN = 0 then goto l1000
  Y = 133
  goto l50

l500:
  ' 500: into a lizard: it moves under the hawkman and eats him (see the
  ' fixes: only the stones' row changes)
  if Hit = 0 then
    B = Y + Q
    call asm HkGet
    if Kd = 36 then
      Bw = Y + 23
      if Bw >= 462 then
        if Bw < 484 then
          B = Bw
          Ch = 35
          PutKeep
        end if
      end if
      Bw = Y + 22
      if Bw >= 462 then
        if Bw < 484 then
          B = Bw
          Ch = 36
          PutKeep
        end if
      end if
      goto l300
    end if
l501:
    ' (see the fixes: no hawkman left behind)
    B = Y
    call asm HkGet
    if Kd = 0 then
      Ch = 32
      PutKeep
    end if
    Y = Y + Q
  end if
  ' 501-507: the crash: a red burst where the hawkman hit, a life
  HawkOff
  B = Y
  Ch = 42
  Cl = 2
  call asm HkPut
  play sound SndCrash
  Hold(4)
  B = Y
  Ch = 32
  PutKeep
  dec TN
  if TN = 0 then goto l1000
  Y = 133
  goto l50

' 1000-1050: the game's end
l1000:
  Ph = 4
  HawkOff
  NewScreen(1, 0)
  Anim = 0
  if Bord = 0 then
    V = 8
  else
    V = 11
  end if
  call asm HkBack
  for Rr = 1 to 23
    fill PSpY count 22 at 5,Rr
  next
  V = VicCol[Tc]
  V = V << 4
  V = V | 11
  Tcf = PAFirst
  Tcn = PACount
  call asm HkColRange
  copy TxOver0 count 19 to vram.name + 37
  copy TxOver1 count 22 to vram.name + 69
  copy TxOver2 count 7 to vram.name + 101
  copy TxOver3 count 21 to vram.name + 133
  copy TxOver4 count 14 to vram.name + 165
  copy TxOver5 count 11 to vram.name + 197
  Nc = 16
  Nr = 6
  NumW = SC
  PNum
  copy TxOver6 count 11 to vram.name + 229
  Nc = 16
  Nr = 7
  PTime
  if SC >= 10000 then
    copy TxWon count 13 to vram.name + 261
  end if
  ShowScreen
  ' (see the fixes: the button let go first)
l1025:
  Pace(1)
  V = Rb | Rd
  if V = 1 then goto l1025
l1030:
  Pace(1)
  if J = 94 then goto l6
  if J = 118 then goto l0
  goto l1030

' World: lines 600-650, once a pass: a stone or a lizard somewhere on the
' bottom row, the skimmer's step (running into the hawkman: Go5, Hit),
' now and then a floater, the border
sub World:
  RndK(22)
  O = Rv + 1
  if O = 22 then O = 0
  RndK(22)
  O = Rv + 1
  if O = 22 then O = 0
  RndK(2)
  D = Rv + 1
  B = O + 462
  if D = 1 then
    Ch = 36
    Cl = 4
  else
    Ch = 35
    Cl = 5
  end if
  call asm HkPut
  ' 605 (see the fixes: not just after the wrap)
  if SK >= 399 then
    B = SK - 3
    Ch = 32
    PutKeep
  end if
  B = SK
  Ch = 33
  PutKeep
  ' 606: the skimmer runs into the hawkman (see the fixes)
  B = SK + 1
  call asm HkGet
  if Kd = 0 then
    Go5 = 1
    Hit = 1
    return
  end if
  SK = SK + 1
  if SK = 418 then
    SK = 396
    B = 416
    Ch = 32
    PutKeep
    B = 417
    PutKeep
    B = 415
    PutKeep
  end if
  ' 610: the head (multicolour on the VIC: black here)
  B = SK
  Ch = 43
  Cl = 0
  call asm HkPut
  Border
  ' 611-616: one pass in ten, a floater in a free cell of rows 7-18
  RndK(10)
  Z = Rv + 1
  if Z <> 5 then return
w612:
  RndK(242)
  F = Rv + 1
  B = F + 154
  call asm HkGet
  if Kd <> 32 then goto w612
w614:
  RndK(7)
  W = Rv + 1
  if W = 7 then goto w614
  B = F + 154
  Ch = 34
  Cl = W
  call asm HkPut
  return
end sub

' Border: lines 625-626 (see the fixes: every pass), under 100 energy the
' border is the screen's yellow, over 100 red
sub Border:
  V = 0
  if E < 100 then V = 1
  if E >= 32768 then V = 1
  if V = 1 then
    if Bord = 0 then
      Bord = 1
      V = 11
      call asm HkBack
    end if
    return
  end if
  if E > 100 then
    if Bord = 1 then
      Bord = 0
      V = 8
      call asm HkBack
    end if
  end if
  return
end sub

' Tongue: lines 100-150: three cells ahead (in red), for 3 energy; what
' it meets (a floater, the skimmer) is eaten
sub Tongue:
  if Y >= 458 then return
  E = E - 3
  ELe0
  if V = 1 then
    Go5 = 1
    return
  end if
  play sound SndTongue
  ' the cells left in this line (see the fixes)
  Bw = Y % 22
  V2 = lowbyte Bw
  V2 = 21 - V2
  X = 1
tg110:
  if X > V2 then goto tg119
  B = Y + X
  call asm HkGet
  if Kd <> 32 then goto tg135
  Ch = 33
  Cl = 2
  call asm HkPut
  Hold(1)
  inc X
  if X <= 3 then goto tg110
tg119:
  Bt = X - 1
tg120:
  if Bt = 0 then return
  B = Y + Bt
  Ch = 32
  PutKeep
  Hold(1)
  dec Bt
  goto tg120
tg135:
  if Kd = 34 then
    E = E + 20
    AddSc(15)
  end if
  if Kd = 33 then
    E = E + 10
    AddSc(5)
  end if
  if Kd = 43 then
    E = E + 10
    AddSc(5)
  end if
  play sound SndGulp
  B = Y + X
  Ch = 42
  PutKeep
  Bt = X
  Hold(4)
  goto tg120
end sub

sub AddSc(u8 N):
  NumW = 65535 - N
  if SC > NumW then
    SC = 65535
  else
    SC = SC + N
  end if
  return
end sub

' ELe0: V = 1 when E <= 0
sub ELe0:
  V = 0
  if E = 0 then V = 1
  if E >= 32768 then V = 1
  return
end sub

' ShowStat: line 58: LIFE: and the lives, the score, the energy (see the
' fixes), in the text colour
sub ShowStat:
  B = 0
  VP(12)
  VP(9)
  VP(6)
  VP(5)
  VP(58)
  NumW = TN
  VNum
  B = 28
  NumW = SC
  VNum
  B = 51
  NumW = E
  if E >= 32768 then NumW = 0
  VNum
  VP(32)
  VP(32)
  return
end sub

' VP: the VIC character C at B in the text colour, B on
sub VP(u8 C):
  Ch = C
  Cl = Tc
  call asm HkPut
  B = B + 1
  return
end sub

' VNum: NumW printed at B as the VIC does (a space, the digits)
sub VNum:
  VP(32)
  Nd = 0
vn_div:
  Bw = NumW % 10
  Dg[Nd] = lowbyte Bw
  inc Nd
  NumW = NumW / 10
  if NumW <> 0 then goto vn_div
vn_put:
  dec Nd
  V = Dg[Nd] + 48
  VP(V)
  if Nd <> 0 then goto vn_put
  return
end sub

' PutKeep: POKE B,Ch (the cell keeps its colour); PutCol: the colour Cl
' at B (the cell keeps its character)
sub PutKeep:
  call asm HkGet
  Cl = Kc
  call asm HkPut
  return
end sub

sub PutCol:
  call asm HkGet
  Ch = Kd
  call asm HkPut
  return
end sub

' HawkGoal: the hawkman's sprite glides to Y's cell (or jumps there when
' it is not next to him)
sub HawkGoal:
  Bw = Y / 22
  V = lowbyte Bw
  Gy = V * 8
  Gy = Gy + 7
  Bw = Y % 22
  V = lowbyte Bw
  Gx = V * 8
  Gx = Gx + 40
  V = 0
  if Gx > Hx then
    V2 = Gx - Hx
  else
    V2 = Hx - Gx
  end if
  if V2 > 8 then V = 1
  if Gy > Hy then
    V2 = Gy - Hy
  else
    V2 = Hy - Gy
  end if
  if V2 > 8 then V = 1
  if V = 1 then
    Hx = Gx
    Hy = Gy
  end if
  return
end sub

' the game's screen: lines 10-35
sub GameScreen:
  NewScreen(0, 0)
  Anim = 1
  V = 8
  call asm HkBack
  ' the text tiles in the text colour
  V = VicCol[Tc]
  V = V << 4
  V = V | 11
  Tcf = TgFirst
  Tcn = TgCount
  call asm HkColRange
  ' 10: the cleared screen: spaces in the text colour
  Ch = 32
  Cl = Tc
  call asm HkEnc
  for Rr = 1 to 23
    fill Tl count 22 at 5,Rr
  next
  ' 20: the clouds (row 4)
  B = 88
  for Rr = 1 to 22
    VP(38)
  next
  ' 21: SCORE: and ENERGY:
  B = 22
  VP(19)
  VP(3)
  VP(15)
  VP(18)
  VP(5)
  VP(58)
  B = 44
  VP(5)
  VP(14)
  VP(5)
  VP(18)
  VP(7)
  VP(25)
  VP(58)
  ' 22: the ground (blue), 30: the stones (green)
  for Rr = 0 to 21
    B = Rr + 484
    Ch = 40
    Cl = 6
    call asm HkPut
    B = Rr + 462
    Ch = 35
    Cl = 5
    call asm HkPut
  next
  ' 35: the skimmer ( !!!+ on row 18)
  B = 396
  VP(32)
  VP(33)
  VP(33)
  VP(33)
  VP(43)
  ShowScreen
  return
end sub

' PNum: NumW in the page's purple digits from column Nc of row Nr, after
' the sign's space
sub PNum:
  put char PSpY at Nc,Nr
  inc Nc
  Nd = 0
pn_div:
  Bw = NumW % 10
  Dg[Nd] = lowbyte Bw
  inc Nd
  NumW = NumW / 10
  if NumW <> 0 then goto pn_div
pn_put:
  dec Nd
  V = Dg[Nd] + PB0
  put char V at Nc,Nr
  inc Nc
  if Nd <> 0 then goto pn_put
  return
end sub

' PTime: VAL(TI$), the hours, minutes and seconds as one number (HHMMSS
' without its leading zeros)
sub PTime:
  Hh = Ts / 3600
  Mm = Ts % 3600
  NumW = Mm % 60
  Mm = Mm / 60
  Rr = lowbyte NumW
  put char PSpY at Nc,Nr
  inc Nc
  if Hh > 0 then
    NumW = Hh
    PNum2
    NumW = Mm
    Pad2
    NumW = Rr
    Pad2
    return
  end if
  if Mm > 0 then
    NumW = Mm
    PNum2
    NumW = Rr
    Pad2
    return
  end if
  NumW = Rr
  PNum2
  return
end sub

' PNum2: NumW's digits (no space); Pad2: two digits
sub PNum2:
  Nd = 0
p2_div:
  Bw = NumW % 10
  Dg[Nd] = lowbyte Bw
  inc Nd
  NumW = NumW / 10
  if NumW <> 0 then goto p2_div
p2_put:
  dec Nd
  V = Dg[Nd] + PB0
  put char V at Nc,Nr
  inc Nc
  if Nd <> 0 then goto p2_put
  return
end sub

sub Pad2:
  Bw = NumW / 10
  V = lowbyte Bw
  V = V + PB0
  put char V at Nc,Nr
  inc Nc
  Bw = NumW % 10
  V = lowbyte Bw
  V = V + PB0
  put char V at Nc,Nr
  inc Nc
  return
end sub

sub CreditsPage:
  Ph = 1
  Hon = 0
  NewScreen(0, 0)
  Anim = 1
  V = 4
  call asm HkBack
  print at 5,2, "THE HAWKMEN OF DINDRIN"
  ' a strip of Dindrin's field
  fill TCl6 count 22 at 5,4
  fill TSp6 count 22 at 5,5
  put char TFl1 at 9,5
  put char TFl3 at 14,5
  put char TFl4 at 19,5
  put char TTg0 at 21,5
  put char TTg0 at 22,5
  put char THd0 at 23,5
  for Rr = 5 to 26
    put char TSt5 at Rr,6
    put char TGnd at Rr,7
  next
  put char TLz4 at 8,6
  put char TLz4 at 17,6
  put char TLz4 at 24,6
  Hx = 48
  Hy = 39
  Gx = 48
  Gy = 39
  Hon = 1
  print at 3,9, "BY ESTEBAN V. AGUILAR JR."
  print at 3,10, "COMPUTE! JUNE 1983, THE"
  print at 3,11, "VIC-20 VERSION. NOTES ON"
  print at 3,12, "THE ATARI AND 64 VERSIONS"
  print at 3,13, "BY CHARLES BRANNON."
  print at 3,15, "STICK: UP CLIMB, DOWN DIVE,"
  print at 3,16, "LEFT BACK. BUTTON: TONGUE."
  print at 3,18, "COLECOVISION: CLAUDE (AN AI"
  print at 3,19, "BY ANTHROPIC), AMY STUDIO."
  print at 3,20, "MUSIC: WINGS OVER DINDRIN."
  print at 8,22, "PRESS THE BUTTON"
  ShowScreen
  play song HkSong once
cp_up:
  Pace(1)
  if Rb = 1 then goto cp_up
cp_wait:
  Pace(1)
  if Rb = 0 then goto cp_wait
  stop song
  return
end sub

' the title: Program 1's screen (green, the name in reverse)
sub TitlePage:
  Ph = 2
  HawkOff
  NewScreen(1, 1)
  Anim = 0
  V = 2
  call asm HkBack
  copy TxTitle count 18 to vram.name + 39
  print at 8,21, "PRESS THE BUTTON"
  ShowScreen
tp_up:
  Pace(1)
  if Rb = 1 then goto tp_up
tp_wait:
  Pace(1)
  if Rb = 0 then goto tp_wait
  ' a new seed from the time spent on the title
  Rt = Tick
  Rs = Rs ^ Rt
  Rt = Rt << 8
  Rs = Rs ^ Rt
  if Rs = 0 then Rs = $3A57
  return
end sub

' NewScreen Bk Fc: a blank screen with the tiles of bank Bk (0 the game's,
' 1 the pages'), the font white (Fc 0) or blue on green (Fc 1)
sub NewScreen(u8 Bk, u8 Fc):
  Rearm
  wait
  nmi off
  display off
  if Fc = 1 then
    fill mode 2 text color with $42
  else
    fill mode 2 text color with $F0
  end if
  if Bk = 0 then
    copy TilePatG count NTilesG to vram.pattern + 1024
    copy TilePatG count NTilesG to vram.pattern + 3072
    copy TilePatG count NTilesG to vram.pattern + 5120
    copy TileColG count NTilesG to vram.color + 1024
    call asm FontTilesG
  else
    copy TilePatP count NTilesP to vram.pattern + 1024
    copy TilePatP count NTilesP to vram.pattern + 3072
    copy TilePatP count NTilesP to vram.pattern + 5120
    copy TileColP count NTilesP to vram.color + 1024
    call asm FontTilesP
  end if
  fill 32 count 768 to vram.name
  Av = 0
  Af = 0
  return
end sub

sub HawkOff:
  Hon = 0
  hide sprite 0
  update sprites
  return
end sub

' ShowScreen: the screen on; then the VDP's status is read once, which
' resets its address latch (an NMI arriving while "screen on" wrote its
' register could leave the latch half-set, and the next VRAM write, the
' hawkman at his start, went astray: seen once in the bot's games)
sub ShowScreen:
  screen on
  nmi off
  call asm HkLatch
  return
end sub

' Pace N: N frames, then the stick: J as the VIC's PEEK(37151) (either
' joystick; right is not read), Rb a button, Rd the stick down
sub Pace(u8 N):
  for Jp = 1 to N
    Frame1
  next
  J = 126
  Rb = 0
  Rd = 0
  V = joypad(1).up | joypad(2).up
  if V = 1 then J = J - 4
  V = joypad(1).down | joypad(2).down
  if V = 1 then
    J = J - 8
    Rd = 1
  end if
  V = joypad(1).left | joypad(2).left
  if V = 1 then J = J - 16
  V = joypad(1).button1 | joypad(2).button1
  V2 = joypad(1).button2 | joypad(2).button2
  V = V | V2
  if V = 1 then
    J = J - 32
    Rb = 1
  end if
  return
end sub

sub Hold(u8 N):
  for Jh = 1 to N
    Frame1
  next
  return
end sub

sub Rearm:
  nmi off
  nmi on
  return
end sub

' Frame1: a frame: TI$, the two views' flip (every 8 frames), the
' hawkman's sprite gliding to his cell (2 pixels the first frame of a
' cell's step, then 1: 8 pixels in 7 frames)
sub Frame1:
  Rearm
  wait
  nmi off
  inc Tick
  inc Fr
  if Fr = 60 then
    Fr = 0
    Ts = Ts + 1
  end if
  if Anim = 1 then
    inc Af
    if Af = 8 then
      Af = 0
      Av = 1 - Av
      call asm HkFlip
    end if
  end if
  if Hon = 1 then
    if Hx < Gx then
      V2 = Gx - Hx
      inc Hx
      if V2 > 6 then inc Hx
    end if
    if Hx > Gx then
      V2 = Hx - Gx
      dec Hx
      if V2 > 6 then dec Hx
    end if
    if Hy < Gy then
      V2 = Gy - Hy
      inc Hy
      if V2 > 6 then inc Hy
    end if
    if Hy > Gy then
      V2 = Hy - Gy
      dec Hy
      if V2 > 6 then dec Hy
    end if
    set sprite 0 to Hy,Hx,Av,1
    update sprites
  end if
  return
end sub

' Rnd16: RND as Rw/65536 (a 16-bit xorshift, 7 9 8)
sub Rnd16:
  Rt = Rs << 7
  Rs = Rs ^ Rt
  Rt = Rs >> 9
  Rs = Rs ^ Rt
  Rt = Rs << 8
  Rs = Rs ^ Rt
  Rw = Rs
  return
end sub

' RndK: Rv = INT(RND(1) * Rk)
sub RndK(u8 Rk):
  Rnd16
  Uq = Rw
  Uq2 = Rk
  Uq = Uq * Uq2
  Uq = Uq >> 16
  Rv = lowword Uq
  return
end sub

